{
  "slug": "ux-superpowers",
  "name": "Ux Superpowers",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "User-centered design methodology for coding agents. Before you brainstorm solutions or write code, UX Superpowers guides you through structured UX discovery: identifying who you're building for (personas), what they're trying to accomplish (jobs-to-be-done), how they experience the problem today (user journey maps), and how you'll know if you succeeded (telemetry and success metrics). Accepts raw user research data (interviews,\nsurveys, support tickets, analytics) or guides discovery from scratch. Produces a UX Discovery Document that anchors all subsequent development. Currently ships 8 skills and works for any software type - web apps, CLIS, APIs, mobile, infrastructure, internal tools, games. Eventually there will be more skills that help in UX Discovery. Designed to complement the Superpowers plugin by owning the \"what and why\" before the \"how\".",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `insight-synthesizer` (Trigger whenever the user says \"compile the discovery doc\", \"synthesize everything into one document\", \"write the UX discovery…), `jobs-to-be-done` (Trigger this skill whenever the user asks \"what are users actually trying to do\", \"what jobs are users…), `persona-builder` (Build me a persona for the primary user of this system, who are the users of this product,…), `research-intake` (Whenever the user hands you raw user-research artifacts — interview transcripts, survey results, NPS verbatims, support tickets, app…), `telemetry-designer` (Use when the user asks how to measure product or feature success, define success metrics, pick a north…), `user-journey` (Use when mapping the end-to-end user experience for any software product, including CLI tools, APIs, SDKs, infrastructure, and…), `ux-discover` (Use BEFORE writing any code, planning, or brainstorming), `ux-validate` (Trigger whenever reviewing a PR, code change, or feature for shipping readiness and a UX Discovery Document exists…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ux-superpowers@claude-community` from `adnanmir123/ux-superpowers`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 8,
    "hook": 1
  },
